<%# Central icon sprite. Rendered once per page and referenced with <use href="#icon-x">.
    Keeps markup readable and avoids repeating path data across templates.

    Conventions every symbol follows, so the set stays visually consistent:
      viewBox="0 0 24 24"        one grid for all icons
      stroke-width="2"           uniform optical weight
      stroke-linecap/linejoin    "round", so corners match across the set
      stroke/fill="currentColor" inherits the surrounding text colour

    Brand marks (facebook, instagram, linkedin, youtube, whatsapp, google) are
    the exception: they are filled, not stroked, and Google keeps its brand
    colours because its guidelines require it.

    focusable="false" keeps the SVG out of the tab order in older Edge/IE, where
    an inline <svg> can otherwise become a keyboard stop. %>
